{"author":{"id":"f943aa1c5ee078b881a8e97535a4e2ccb401d01ca00f4128126befa9cca58a32"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792577111,"nonce":"T6el/1nQAhs+pI4hNizdgRzUqe0=","metadata":{"github-url":"https://github.com/guilbep/git-board/issues/32","origin":"github","sync:github.com/guilbep/git-board:id":"I_kwDOUJip488AAAABYya0XQ","sync:github.com/guilbep/git-board:labels":"","sync:github.com/guilbep/git-board:number":"32","sync:github.com/guilbep/git-board:status":"open","sync:github.com/guilbep/git-board:text":"4a16572be743f84d398f37bb7131393f03939ee0f8044cc5b86de6600ab0362d","sync:github.com/guilbep/git-board:title":"bridge: a failed repository check after a not-found marks a bug gone","sync:github.com/guilbep/git-board:url":"https://github.com/guilbep/git-board/issues/32"},"title":"bridge: a failed repository check after a not-found marks a bug gone","message":"Found in the native-fields final review; it predates native-fields. In both adapters, `confirm()` (bridge/github/remote.go, bridge/gitlab/remote.go) checks the repository after a write or read answers \"not found\". When that check fails too, `confirm()` wraps the original not-found, and the engine marks the bug gone for good: every later pull and push skips it.\n\nFix: when the repository check fails, return its own error, not the not-found, so the bug stays synced and the run reports the failure. Add a test with a reader that can't see the repository.","files":null}]}